# Documentation taxonomy (Diataxis-adapted)

All docs under `docs/` must be classified into one of these page types:

- `component`: canonical reference for one Figma component (`docs/components/*.md`, excluding `overview.md`)
- `overview`: navigation/index page for a section (`**/overview.md`)
- `foundation`: token-driven foundations page (`docs/foundations/*.md`, excluding `overview.md`)
- `workflow`: process/runbook page (`docs/get-started/*.md`, `docs/a11y/*.md`, or explicit workflow folders)

## Metadata contract

Use `frontmatter-contract.mdc` for required frontmatter fields and allowed values.
This rule defines taxonomy scope and page intent boundaries, not field validation details.

## Scope discipline

- A `component` page must not include runbook/process instructions.
- A `workflow` page must not duplicate full component reference tables.
- An `overview` page must summarize and link; it should not duplicate deep specs from component pages.
- A `foundation` page should describe token families and links to generated inventories, not component-specific API details.

## Cross-rule references

- Component pages must also follow `component-doc-structure.mdc`.
- Global integrity and no-invention behavior is defined in `ds-docs-guardrails.mdc`.
